{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"D0+D1 are architecturally faithful and the reviewed implementation is ready to proceed.\n\n1. D0 contract fidelity: confirmed. The descriptor has the declared 22 slots, excludes hash/root markers from node identity, uses the descriptor content hash as the transitional domain separator, records the canonical value table, splits vector/list classes, applies NFC through the pinned Dart seam, resets framing/index state per root, and enforces the specified validation and macro-detection rules.\n\n2. D1 resolver: confirmed. Frame depth, source parameter positions, inner-to-outer lookup, rightmost-wins duplicate binding, free-name preservation, cycle detection, and `[source-eid lexical-context]` memoization match §3. The memo is explicit and tested as identity-neutral.\n\n3. `:vector`/`:list` split: blessed without amendment. These values are observably distinct, so merging them would create an unsound identity collision. The descriptor, canonical table, resolver output, and tests consistently preserve the distinction.\n\n4. D2–D3 impact: no architectural rework is required. D2 must retain the split and consume the resolved semantic graph; D3 must encode the distinct classes, signed zero, integral-double/int64 rule, and tag-specific Merkle slots. D3 must also replace the documented transitional descriptor digest with the settled canonical digest while keeping the descriptor itself stable.\n\nSIGN-OFF GRANTED for committing D0+D1 on debruijn-impl and proceeding to D2"}}
